   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Complete recipe recovered from SI Appendix (Detailed Methods + Table S1). This is a fully defined phosphate-buffered minimal medium: NH4Cl (N), K2HPO4/NaH2PO4 (P/buffer), MgSO4, CaCl2, and a defined 6-salt trace-metal mix (B, Cu, Zn, Mn, Ni, Mo), with ferrous salt as Fe source and EDTA as chelator to set unchelated Fe (Fe-replete 30 uM / intermediate 650 nM / severe Fe-limited 38 nM; 90 uM EDTA added for the severe condition modeled here). No vitamins and no reductant are used (prototrophic Pseudomonas grown aerobically in baffled flasks with sponge caps, 220 rpm, 30C). Correction: the current"
